{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":214634,"duration_api_ms":348699,"num_turns":17,"result":"All acceptance criteria are met. The deliverable is complete — both `docs/validation_scenarios.md` (8 literature-backed scenarios) and `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_validation_suite.rs` (8 executable probes + summary runner) are fully implemented and all tests pass 8/8.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"change_summary\": \"Literature-backed validation scenario envelopes and executable test suite are complete. docs/validation_scenarios.md documents 8 scenarios (VS-01 through VS-08) covering chemistry (cycling, aeration, pH swing, source-water differentiation, denitrification), ecology (algae-plant competition), and animal behavior (shrimp breeding, stocking crash). Each scenario includes a rationale paragraph, peer-reviewed literature citations (Hovanec & DeLong 1996, Colt 2006, Brewer & Goldman 1976, Stumm & Morgan 1996, Tropea et al. 2015, Tilman 1982, Seitzinger 1988, Timmons & Ebeling 2010), expected qualitative outcomes, confidence rating (high or medium), and envelope bounds. The e2e_validation_suite.rs test file implements all 8 probes with deterministic seeded runs, multi-checkpoint envelope assertions, and a summary runner that reports pass/fail per scenario with confidence tier breakdown. A minor type alias refactor (ProbeFn) in the summary runner improves readability. All 9 tests pass (8 probes + 1 summary), clippy is clean, and formatting is verified.\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Explore project structure to understand existing validation infrastructure, harness APIs, scenario definitions, and provenance metadata system\",\n      \"order\": 0,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Read docs/validation_scenarios.md to verify 8 scenarios with literature citations, rationale, expected outcomes, confidence ratings, and envelope bounds\",\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n